cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its derived artifacts, please cite it as below."
title: "Spatially blocked pluvial-flood susceptibility learning on the H3 DGGS using heterogeneous open public data"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-08"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Coucou2016/pluvial-flood-risk-DGGS-H3"
abstract: >-
  An open-evidence H3 discrete-global-grid protocol for urban pluvial-flood
  susceptibility screening. The main target is a binary union of heterogeneous
  public evidence (DEP stormwater polygons, NYC 311 street-flooding complaints,
  USGS Hurricane Ida high-water marks); evaluation uses H3 parent-block spatial
  cross-validation with metre guard bands and spatial-block bootstrap confidence
  intervals. A strict, never-trained FloodNet external check did not establish
  event-level skill and is reported as a core negative result. This is a
  screening/susceptibility study, not a calibrated depth, probability, or
  flood-event product, and it does not reproduce any proprietary index.
keywords:
  - pluvial flood
  - flood susceptibility
  - H3
  - discrete global grid system
  - spatial cross-validation
  - machine learning
  - open data
